{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect","id":932461,"title":"Is \"My Clan Discipline for Yours\" as common as PCs seem to expect?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-16T04:09:40-07:00","id":932461,"title":"Is \"My Clan Discipline for Yours\" as common as PCs seem to expect?","content":"There is an undercurrent of expectation that trading one clan discipline for another is a fair trade and should happen among PCs, particularly in community-based games. I'm not so sure this makes sense from an in-universe perspective, but I can't put my finger on why. It just feels wrong. What are your guy's thoughts on the subject?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T04:50:56-07:00","id":932468,"title":"","content":"Well, why does it feel wrong? Is it possible that this is an expectation from Masquerade that slipped over, where clan disciplines were considered sacred secrets to not be shared? Remember, in 2e you don't even need the blood of a Nosferatu to learn Nightmare - if your sire knows it, then you can learn it from them. Even the vitae you need to drink can come from anyone that knows the Signature Discipline. And that's not touching on the number of bloodlines with signature disciplines for a fourth. The big &quot;secret disciplines&quot; in Requiem are the covenant magics. Sharing Oaths, Laws, Coils, Cruac or Theban with outsiders carries still penalties and taboos. But Requiem has never restricted signature disciplines in any way beyond what's in the 2e core.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that you might have been feeling some aversion to the idea of casually swapping vitae among players - willing blood bonds and addiction seems crazy to a number of players. Could this be it?<br /> <br /> As for me and my games? I have never once had an time with it being heavily restricted. Clans, even when organized, simply don't have the power to regulate Disciplines in that manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T07:34:53-07:00","id":932498,"title":"","content":"The way I run things, Disciplines are a meta-game concept. The characters don't conceive of ten discrete powers each with five levels of mastery, and the idea of &quot;swapping signature disciplines&quot; wouldn't really occur to most vampires in my games. There is, however, a certain awareness that Vitae is power, and the Vitae of different Clans makes them powerful in different ways. The wild blood of the Gangrel makes them close to their Beasts and allows them to commune with and even take the form of animals. The powerful blood of the Ventrue makes their gaze hypnotic and forces man and beast alike to obey their commands. The horrid blood of the Nosferatu makes them easy to miss and terrible to behold. Etc. A vampire of one Clan may desire the power of another Clan's blood, but they may or may not consider the risk of blood bond worth the power. The kind of mutual trust required to knowingly and willingly exchange Vitae is rare among vampires. More often, powers of the blood might be discovered accidentally after being unknowingly or unwillingly blood bound, stolen through Diablerie, or taken as payment for a service rendered to a lesser vampire who's blood you don't believe potent enough to bind you. But I don't think blood sharing within a coterie is all that unheard of. Certainly something I would allow PCs to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T07:43:00-07:00","id":932503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932498#post932498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I run things, Disciplines are a meta-game concept. The characters don't conceive of ten discrete powers each with five levels of mastery, and the idea of &quot;swapping signature disciplines&quot; wouldn't really occur to most vampires in my games. There is, however, a certain awareness that Vitae is power, and the Vitae of different Clans makes them powerful in different ways. The wild blood of the Gangrel makes them close to their Beasts and allows them to commune with and even take the form of animals. The powerful blood of the Ventrue makes their gaze hypnotic and forces man and beast alike to obey their commands. The horrid blood of the Nosferatu makes them easy to miss and terrible to behold. Etc. A vampire of one Clan may desire the power of another Clan's blood, but they may or may not consider the risk of blood bond worth the power. The kind of mutual trust required to knowingly and willingly exchange Vitae is rare among vampires. More often, powers of the blood might be discovered accidentally after being unknowingly or unwillingly blood bound, stolen through Diablerie, or taken as payment for a service rendered to a lesser vampire who's blood you don't believe potent enough to bind you. But I don't think blood sharing within a coterie is all that unheard of. Certainly something I would allow PCs to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> +1 pretty much sums it up perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T09:09:31-07:00","id":932535,"title":"","content":"It isn't very common in my games because the players tended to view it as rather pointless to even bother distinguishing between clans if everyone's power spread is uniform and clans leadership are just fine with clan mates freely trading clan signatures as minor favors. That doesn't mean you didn't encounter a Nosferatu with a rank or two in Auspex or a Gangrel with Majesty but it would be extremely rare to see a Mekhet with Dominate at level 5 or a Daeva turning into mist. Personally I don't see clans particularly wanting their most powerful abilities to be in the hands of outsiders so they would discourage the creation of or outright eliminate such aberrations publicly advertising their repertoire frequently based on trumped up accusations like diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T10:31:23-07:00","id":932556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932535#post932535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't very common in my games because the players tended to view it as rather pointless to even bother distinguishing between clans if everyone's power spread is uniform and clans leadership are just fine with clan mates freely trading clan signatures as minor favors. That doesn't mean you didn't encounter a Nosferatu with a rank or two in Auspex or a Gangrel with Majesty but it would be extremely rare to see a Mekhet with Dominate at level 5 or a Daeva turning into mist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can definitely see where you're coming from there. I think in practice my games look similar. I don't build very many NPCs with out-of-Clan Disciplines, and when I do it's usually just a dot or two. Enough to meet a Devotion prerequisite maybe, but usually not more than that. If you see a Deva turn to mist, you can pretty much assume they're part of a Bloodline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932535#post932535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I don't see clans particularly wanting their most powerful abilities to be in the hands of outsiders so they would discourage the creation of or outright eliminate such aberrations publicly advertising their repertoire frequently based on trumped up accusations like diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Myself, I don't see Clans as United enough as social constructs to have collective desires like keeping their powers out of the hands of other Clans. I could see bloodlines or dynasties having those kinds of attitudes, but Clans are just too broad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T13:41:48-07:00","id":932616,"title":"","content":"Vampires in general tend to be very selfish and hoard power of all kinds. I could see swapping like this but mostly only when they each see themselves as somehow cheating the other guy by gaining more than they give.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T00:00:28-07:00","id":932821,"title":"","content":"Most community game players are looking for dots on their sheet that they can't get easily because dots are forever but a character that owes you a couple boons might up and vanish forever into the internet wilds at random. IMO I don't care because if I'm playing a Mekhet and someone wants to trade some Auspex lessons for some Animalism or a boon then whatever. They'll stick around or they won't and I don't actually loose anything irreplacable if they vanish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T00:04:42-07:00","id":932823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932821#post932821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most community game players are looking for dots on their sheet that they can't get easily because dots are forever but a character that owes you a couple boons might up and vanish forever into the internet wilds at random. IMO I don't care because if I'm playing a Mekhet and someone wants to trade some Auspex lessons for some Animalism or a boon then whatever. They'll stick around or they won't and I don't actually loose anything irreplacable if they vanish.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You don't need lessons to learn animalism by the way, it's only the clan-exclusive ones (dominate, nightmare, protean, majesty and ausepx) that require lessons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T00:10:29-07:00","id":932824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932823#post932823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need lessons to learn animalism by the way, it's only the clan-exclusive ones (dominate, nightmare, protean, majesty and ausepx) that require lessons.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW sure, but some communities house rule non-in clans to be more time consuming to learn in the interest of fostering player interaction. Sure I can learn Animalism if I want to bank XP and spend a couple months rolling some dice to cover blue book time, but why bother when I can trade Auspex for some? I don't loose anything but the banked time already spent learning and everyone wants a little Auspex cause it's handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T00:22:17-07:00","id":932828,"title":"","content":"RAW, there's no such thing as lessons. Just taking vitae. The fluff suggests the Disciplines just manifest. Which I kind of like. Keeps things more mysterious and uncertain IC even if on a meta level we know exactly how stuff works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T00:53:39-07:00","id":932833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect#post932461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an undercurrent of expectation that trading one clan discipline for another is a fair trade and should happen among PCs, particularly in community-based games. I'm not so sure this makes sense from an in-universe perspective, but I can't put my finger on why. It just feels wrong. What are your guy's thoughts on the subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only real fluff on the matter I recall is in the Ventrue clanbook. There the POV character in piece on the Domm\u00e9 Cohen reports that other Venture of her city are &quot;disgusted&quot; she teaches Dominate to non-Lords. Of course, this is about the Ventrue who perhaps have a different attitude to their Clan Discipline being shared than the Gangrel might, especially given the nature of that Discipline. Furthermore, the attitude of the Ventrue of that city does not need to be representative, but at least there is precedent for signature Disciplines being shared leading to at least some degree of indignation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932828#post932828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, there's no such thing as lessons. Just taking vitae. The fluff suggests the Disciplines just manifest. Which I kind of like. Keeps things more mysterious and uncertain IC even if on a meta level we know exactly how stuff works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for Clan Disciplines that are learned Out-of-Clan:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core, pg. 83</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When learned out-of-clan, Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, and Protean require <b>teachers</b>, as they are tied deeply to the blood of the clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Also, while they are 1e material, we have multiple instances of Kindred being taught or being teacher in setting material; like Earth Baines learning Obfuscate in the Chicago books, the Domm\u00e9 Cohen mentioned above and an entire Academy (!) dedicated to teaching Dominate, also from the Ventrue clanbook.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T02:14:19-07:00","id":932845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932828#post932828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, there's no such thing as lessons. Just taking vitae. The fluff suggests the Disciplines just manifest. Which I kind of like. Keeps things more mysterious and uncertain IC even if on a meta level we know exactly how stuff works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, that doesn't explains Cru\u00e1c, Theban, Coils, Oaths or Laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T03:29:13-07:00","id":932857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932828#post932828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, there's no such thing as lessons. Just taking vitae. The fluff suggests the Disciplines just manifest. Which I kind of like. Keeps things more mysterious and uncertain IC even if on a meta level we know exactly how stuff works.</div> </div> </div> </div> Page 83 says that you don't need teachers for in-clan disciplines or common disciplines. You do need teachers for signature disciplines and covenant disciplines, however. Or for any unique disciplines that may appear.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, if we go by the new rules here on learning disciplines, then you could theoretically learn bloodline signature powers as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T06:14:47-07:00","id":932876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932857#post932857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Page 83 says that you don't need teachers for in-clan disciplines or common disciplines. You do need teachers for signature disciplines and covenant disciplines, however. Or for any unique disciplines that may appear.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, if we go by the new rules here on learning disciplines, then you could theoretically learn bloodline signature powers as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>David Hill actually said this is possible. Bloodline Devotions (but not Disciplines) can be learned outside the bloodline, but require teaching and Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T08:20:51-07:00","id":932909,"title":"","content":"There are a few reasons you might not want to swap signature disciplines There's always the risk of vitae addiction and a blood bond, and having someone bonded to you can cause as many issues as being bound to someone. A recent Ventrue character of mine refused to teach anyone Dominate because he didn't want to be responsible for them possibly abusing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T08:45:31-07:00","id":932922,"title":"","content":"That last bit is important. Someone asked my Mekhet to trade Auspex for Majesty and my gut response was &quot;wait, so I'm trading you *everyone's* secrets in exchange for being more well liked? If you find out secrets via Auspex am I responsible?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean the issue isn't him finding out my Mekhet's secrets. I figure any Ancillae or older Mekhet with high Auspex understands that secrets *will* get out and plans around that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:20:37-07:00","id":932978,"title":"","content":"If you don't want your character to trade disciplines like that, then don't do it. You devalue your character's usefulness to the group when everyone has Auspex. It depends on the setting if whether or not your character would be held accountable for others' discipline use. Furthermore not all disciplines are equally useful or viable so a 1 for 1 trade is not equitable. Personally I'd say the one giving Auspex for Majesty is about an even trade, but anyone giving either of those two for ANY other clan signature is getting ripped off. Your Mekhet should hold out for more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T14:26:15-07:00","id":933056,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is common or expected at all. Your players might want to swap, but again, I don't feel it's common practice. <br /> <br /> There are huge risks. The blood bond and vitae addiction have been mentioned. There might be city rules about two way blood bonds. Perversions to worry about. Also Being responsible for what happens after you give them that power. <br /> <br /> raw: You do have to have blood and a teacher to learn a clan specific discipline, that shouldn't be under debate.<br /> You do have to have a teacher for the covenant coils and sorceries<br /> <br /> Side note: I do play with vampires knowing and having named the disciplines. It seems for all the years that vampires have been around they would have come up with something better than, &quot;that scary thing Nosferatu can do&quot; Though in that same breath I don't have them know that there are 5 levels of it. Just different masteries. Like a vampire would say, &quot;I have mastered Majesty.&quot; Just like the Ordo have named their scales and mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T09:52:35-07:00","id":935104,"title":"","content":"In my Requiem game on Rpol, When a young ventrue was thinking about trading tutoring in Dominate for Tutoring in Protean. to a unbound Gangrel her sire advised her to &quot;Sell Your Birthright DEARLY&quot; <br /> <br /> Not &quot;Not at all&quot; But to be aware once taught, they could teach it to a 3rd party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:34:37-07:00","id":935125,"title":"","content":"Nothing wrong with players doing it... but keep in mind that vampires mutually swapping blood is called &quot;perversion&quot; by Kindred culture in general, and looked down on. Probably because of the behavior that kind of weird love tends to produce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:39:50-07:00","id":935408,"title":"","content":"I've never seen it in a game. I've never seen it in Requiem fiction, where sharing of personal Disciplines seems like something so rude to ask of another vampire, not to mention the weirdness of asking to be blood bonded to another vampire.<br /> <br /> If there's an undercurrent of expectation I think it would be from players who want more Disciplines for their characters and don't plan on playing out the side effects of the Vinculum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T18:55:35-07:00","id":935412,"title":"","content":"Blood bonds are so much fun to roleplay though. My last vampire character was in vinculum to 5 different vampires at one point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T04:36:23-08:00","id":1163865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=932498#post932498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I run things, Disciplines are a meta-game concept. The characters don't conceive of ten discrete powers each with five levels of mastery, and the idea of &quot;swapping signature disciplines&quot; wouldn't really occur to most vampires in my games. There is, however, a certain awareness that Vitae is power, and the Vitae of different Clans makes them powerful in different ways. The wild blood of the Gangrel makes them close to their Beasts and allows them to commune with and even take the form of animals. The powerful blood of the Ventrue makes their gaze hypnotic and forces man and beast alike to obey their commands. The horrid blood of the Nosferatu makes them easy to miss and terrible to behold. Etc. A vampire of one Clan may desire the power of another Clan's blood, but they may or may not consider the risk of blood bond worth the power. The kind of mutual trust required to knowingly and willingly exchange Vitae is rare among vampires. More often, powers of the blood might be discovered accidentally after being unknowingly or unwillingly blood bound, stolen through Diablerie, or taken as payment for a service rendered to a lesser vampire who's blood you don't believe potent enough to bind you. But I don't think blood sharing within a coterie is all that unheard of. Certainly something I would allow PCs to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a cool concept and I loved it, I used something like this on past tables and I still suggest this when I perceive that the table has too many powerplayers.<br /> <br /> But after my reading of Bloodline The Legendaries (Players Bloodline), I came to the conclusion that vampires do know that disciplines are ten discrete powers each with different levels of mastery.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:56:40-08:00","id":1163945,"title":"","content":"in a game I ran on Rpol, a PC Ventrue wound up trading Dominate to a Gangrel poacher, for being taught the basics of protean.<br /> is that a fair exchange?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:18:18-08:00","id":1163951,"title":"","content":"Entirely depends on the characters involved and how they see it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't do the trade, though. The Gangrel could use that first dot of Dominate to mind-control the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue could use that first dot of Protean to... sleep in the dirt.<br /> <br /> Doesn't seem like a fair exchange of risk to me, unless that Ventrue desperately needed a Haven before sunrise.<br /> <br /> Given that he has Dominate, he is probably not that desperate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:51:37-08:00","id":1163981,"title":"","content":"I think it is an excellent question, but more to let the characters answer than to have a meta-answer.<br /> <br /> There is no meta-reason to not let it happen, neither for mechanics nor setting. Even most Bloodlines aren't as closed as Masquerade's Clans became. Vampires are individuals first, and you can't expect that a person you actually <i>cursed</i> will hold to your expectations just because you're &quot;daddy&quot;. I doubt that vampires would have such expectations as a whole.<br /> <br /> But then, there are several consequences, questions, and even more than players, the characters have those questions and think their personal answers. They also live in relatively isolated communities, so each city can deliver its own answers without regard to a &quot;global&quot; view. That's the most important thing, you shouldn't have too many global rules, or any at all, but you can have a lot of quirks for specific cities.<br /> <br /> A character that is looked down by peers for trading a signature discipline shows two things. First, that at <u>this</u> city it isn't viewed in a good light. Second, that it isn't a crime, either. But it can be somewhere else, as both individuals and communities find their answers to those questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:19:03-08:00","id":1163994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1163951#post1163951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ventrue could use that first dot of Protean to... sleep in the dirt.<br /> <br /> Doesn't seem like a fair exchange of risk to me, unless that Ventrue desperately needed a Haven before sunrise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could actually see a certain type of Ventrue willing to take that risk. After all, one of, if not <i>the</i>, greatest weakness a Kindred faces is the helplessness and vulnerability of daysleep. A control-obsessed Lord could very easily see Protean 1 as a way of taking back the power to choose where they will refuge from the sun each day, rather than having to obsessively cultivate a stable (and thus findable) haven.<br /> <br /> You could take it even further, using it as a shell game to distract enemies. They spend months planning an assault, painstakingly tracking down your Haven, noting escape routes, figuring out defenses and traps, building up their resources until they finally storm the haven (taking heavy losses) and find...that you're <i>not there</i>, because you're <i>actually </i>sleeping beneath the Dairy Queen parking lot six blocks away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:42:38-08:00","id":1163998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1163945#post1163945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in a game I ran on Rpol, a PC Ventrue wound up trading Dominate to a Gangrel poacher, for being taught the basics of protean.<br /> is that a fair exchange?</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual exchange here is one year of a first stage Vindiculim and Blood Adiction (if you're not already under one of those) for access to an ability that would otherwise be unavailable, I'm inclined to say yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:03:06-08:00","id":1164052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1163994#post1163994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could actually see a certain type of Ventrue willing to take that risk. After all, one of, if not <i>the</i>, greatest weakness a Kindred faces is the helplessness and vulnerability of daysleep. A control-obsessed Lord could very easily see Protean 1 as a way of taking back the power to choose where they will refuge from the sun each day, rather than having to obsessively cultivate a stable (and thus findable) haven.<br /> <br /> You could take it even further, using it as a shell game to distract enemies. They spend months planning an assault, painstakingly tracking down your Haven, noting escape routes, figuring out defenses and traps, building up their resources until they finally storm the haven (taking heavy losses) and find...that you're <i>not there</i>, because you're <i>actually </i>sleeping beneath the Dairy Queen parking lot six blocks away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a Ventrue potentially trading Dominate for Protean but not a control obsessed one. They would be surrendering their free will to someone else, potentially indefinitely in exchange for further empowering the Gangrel to exercise even more control over the Ventrue in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T18:43:36-08:00","id":1164132,"title":"","content":"I know that Vampires play fast and loose with their bodies because ... well blood, violation, and horror themes... but in real life, would such trades not suffer the inhibiting effects one might associate with using ones body in sexual ways?<br /> <br /> I take a weird pleasure in reminding guys who declare that if they were women, they'd find it easy to elevate their social status because they could just 'bare all' on camera and such to obtain views, fame, what have you, that if they were indeed women, they'd be as conservative with their bodies as they're now. (Apologies for the proliferation of commas in the previous sentence.) Gay-for-pay is a thing, to my knowledge, but I noticed upon been informed of such, the guy rarely sets up a camera and starts making bank. Actual hurdles in plying that trade aside, it seems they believe they would until they can, and then they don't.<br /> <br /> All this nonsense just to say, perhaps PC's do it because the players are playing. The characters of the world may not like the idea of surrendering themselves for clear gains for the same reason the lads above shy away. Some clearly do do it, but we aren't all engaged in the sex industry; likewise for experimenting which may not be as common as some think and more common than others think.<br /> <br /> On paper, even IC, it might be a purely utilitarian trade but I'd play it that it is rare (especially among the neonate and ancilla), because when push comes to shove, sharing YOUR blood is intimate and you've got this requiem thing sorted, so you don't NEED that power. Maybe you need to think about this, because what if you don't REALLY want it? What if it is a trap or a fad? Are we sure there are no side-effects? The others want it but are you so easily led? No, you'll take your time and consider this. Besides, you're immortal, you can try it later, no need to rush. You'll have unlimited power, but tonight, might just get a bite to eat, ya know?<br /> <br /> /ramble<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T14:25:21-08:00","id":1166534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1163865#post1163865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a cool concept and I loved it, I used something like this on past tables and I still suggest this when I perceive that the table has too many powerplayers.<br /> <br /> But after my reading of Bloodline The Legendaries (Players Bloodline), I came to the conclusion that vampires do know that disciplines are ten discrete powers each with different levels of mastery.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which part of BtL exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T15:46:14-08:00","id":1166552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1166534#post1166534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which part of BtL exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>End of page 126 and the beginning of page 127.<br /> Disciplines and Devotions.<br /> <br /> They seen to reference that these vampires know the diferences between each discipline and that they know that their &quot;coolest powers&quot; (late levels) take too long to Develop.<br /> Also tells about some of them who are persistent enough to get such mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T17:12:59-08:00","id":1166571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1164132#post1164132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that Vampires play fast and loose with their bodies because .../ramble</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. I used to play WoW back in the day and when I wanted to quickly get back to town, I might jump off a cliff or find a troll to cave in my skull for me instead of running back on foot. It's an easy choice to make when actual consequences don't factor in.<br /> <br /> Vinculum is a nasty thing and most players won't find it fun to lose control of their own character. If your players insist on these things, you may want to reintroduce them to what the Vinculum truly is by way of a pathetic, abused NPC Thrall. Trying of course to convey that this is how they could end up by playing such dangerous games.<br /> Maybe the NPC who facilitated the trade lets his new power over the PC go to his head and complications ensue.<br /> <br /> If the PC's are engaging in the Perversion or are fine with a one-way bond among PC's then you all might want to take another look at what type of chronicle you are wanting to play because it seriously changes coterie dynamics even with just a 1st stage bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T19:46:41-08:00","id":1166584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1166571#post1166571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the PC's are engaging in the Perversion or are fine with a one-way bond among PC's....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is what I am getting at. The players might be fine with it, but I'd be curious how it is rationalised away in-character?<br /> <br /> I suppose if I was given good reasons, that would feel realistic for those with an incredibly limited perspective (i.e not players of a game, but denizens of a world), then I could see trades been more common. Any thoughts on that side of things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  Screw it, let's open pandora's box. 12-10-2017, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T20:13:08-08:00","id":1166588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1166584#post1166584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The players might be fine with it, but I'd be curious how it is rationalised away in-character?</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>The characters are involved in some way. A pair of sisters, Embraced by different clans who still feel more loyalty to their blood than their Blood. Or the old standard of a couple of lovers who want to share everything, damn the consequences.</li> <li>They're fresh neonates who don't really &quot;get&quot; the consequences of a blood bond quite yet, but <i>do </i>get that their coterie buddy can do cool stuff they can't. Share and share alike, right?</li> <li>They have a plan that requires the use of a specific Discipline that's out-of-clan for them, and they consider the risks of teaching someone else their clan's power and/or a potential blood bond to be more acceptable than trusting another vampire with a part in the plan.</li> </ul>I'm not sure if I agree with the idea that sharing your Vitae with another vampire to trade Disciplines is all exploitative or physically intimate (or, at least, that the average Kindred would see it that way). After all, many (if not most) vampires make ghouls, or spill Vitae as part of various Disciplines or covenant perks. Plus, we already <i>have</i> the sex metaphor for vampires: it's the Kiss, and it's something (almost...) every vampire engages in all the time. Indeed, nothing says that two vampires &quot;swapping Blood&quot; need to even bite each other- pour your Vitae into two shot glasses, clink 'em together and bottom's up. There <i>is </i>a taboo against giving the Kiss to another Kindred, but that's more because &quot;it's what we do to the food.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T21:47:31-08:00","id":1166607,"title":"","content":"I've never seen it done in the fiction, or can't recall it happening even among close friends (and you don't really blood bond close friends unless you want to ruin the relationship).<br /> <br /> Usually with the Beast, with the nature of the All Night's Society it gets drilled into vampires early that their powers are going to be the only thing keeping them going and keeping them from being taken advantage of in the worst of ways. And their own nature isn't exactly encouraging generosity and trust. Look at things like the assorted blood sorceries and the Coils and Scales. Everyone seems to be able to learn them, but unless you're really tight with that covenant they're going to tear you to pieces. The only thing that likely keeps clans from doing similarly is that they're not as well organized.<br /> <br /> But PCs are by their nature special. Even if you as ST run a setting where characters are all 'on the same level' and the PCs aren't meant to stand out, they'd do so by the very fact that they are played by people other than you.<br /> <br /> I'd probably let the PCs know that their instincts cringe away from the idea but leave it up to them.<br /> <br /> Realistically, the players in my group would be more likely to seek it out from NPCs, either stealing it from them or perhaps from a superior or lover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-11-2017, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T11:36:51-08:00","id":1166752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1166588#post1166588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>The characters are involved in some way. A pair of sisters, Embraced by different clans who still feel more loyalty to their blood than their Blood. Or the old standard of a couple of lovers who want to share everything, damn the consequences.</li> <li>They're fresh neonates who don't really &quot;get&quot; the consequences of a blood bond quite yet, but <i>do </i>get that their coterie buddy can do cool stuff they can't. Share and share alike, right?</li> <li>They have a plan that requires the use of a specific Discipline that's out-of-clan for them, and they consider the risks of teaching someone else their clan's power and/or a potential blood bond to be more acceptable than trusting another vampire with a part in the plan.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>First off, in replying to you, I figured out how to do lists on this forum. Will be handy, thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><ul><li>'The characters are involved in some way.' Yeah, that sounds okay. They are attached at the hip. How common is that though; as a justification for someone sharing clan secrets, sure, but as a justification for the general trade...Doesn't strike me as plausible that it is common. See nofather's points above for why.</li> <li>'Fresh neonates' would have very little knowledge of the blood. Why would they assume it was even possible? If they do know (encouraged by bored ancilla) and want to do it, they run into the problems I said before. Doubt would constrain them, and since there is no pressure, they might hold off. A some point, they cease being so fresh. If society permitted it, they would be more likely but all it takes is a Sire telling them it is taboo for them to not. Again, I can see it happening and I am not trying to dismiss your point. I'm just exploring it to assess how compelling it is, how common it might be, and such. As it stands, fresh neonates aren't likely to be the reason it is popular or done, so it still sounds like a rare trade. Using the Kiss as a sex metaphor though, it might be more common if vampires grouped together to survive ( i.e. neonates) have a tendency to 'eat' each other. They more or less exchange with each other by accident. Do Vampires want to 'eat' each other in this way? Is the Man more the cause for this, trying to reignite its sexual aspect? All this modifies likelihood but so far, I think trade proposals would be met with a raised eyebrow by good vampire society.</li> <li>The utilitarian perspective. Again, against all the doubt and danger, how often will vamps act according to their rational side instead of bowing out? Would this be the basis for widespread use. This comes back to your points challenging the intimacy of the exchange. I agree, insofar that it doesn't feel wrong, it will most likely come down to pure logic. However, surrendering your blood, letting another drink from you, even if not directly, seems like it would feel wrong to the Take-Take side of the beast. Yes, they make ghouls and fuel powers by letting blood, but ghouls are extensions of the beast and powers likewise. The beast reacts differently to its own and I think it would manifest feelings of dread/disgust at allowing others to 'eat' it. In sum, even if it wasn't sexual, it might still disturb the closest thing a vampire has to instincts.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> All in all, I still see it as rare. Happens, for lots of reasons, but all those reasons together amount to a sizeable minority, not a majority. In fact, the more common, the more likely it is shunned and looked down upon. In my opinion.<br /> <br /> (I promise... I'm not a prude... :P )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:31:14-08:00","id":1166791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1166752#post1166752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all, I still see it as rare. Happens, for lots of reasons, but all those reasons together amount to a sizeable minority, not a majority. In fact, the more common, the more likely it is shunned and looked down upon. In my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sure. I never meant to imply I thought it would be <i>common</i>. I was just spitballing simple reasons that could overcome any societal &quot;shunning&quot; or taboo. I mean, look at how may taboos living human society has...and how it has just as many people willing, and eager, to give those taboos the finger. I definitely know people who, if told sharing blood was a bad idea, would pretty much <i>immediately</i> go out and do it. &quot;You're not my real sire!&quot;<br /> <br /> One of my big instincts when it comes to world building and fiction is that the &quot;rules&quot; are there to give you a baseline, so that when you decide to break them you'll be more likely to think of a good reason. &quot;Here is the box. Now think outside of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1166607#post1166607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But PCs are by their nature special. Even if you as ST run a setting where characters are all 'on the same level' and the PCs aren't meant to stand out, they'd do so by the very fact that they are played by people other than you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I definitely see it as simply another option to mark the PCs out as special. Like how a neonate PC likely will amass skills, connections and Disciplines far faster than an NPC elder that's canonically been around for far longer. Nobody <i>has</i><i> to</i> do it, just like nobody <i>has to</i> join a Covenant and rise up through the ranks.<br /> <br /> If the players want their characters to all share Disciplines and blood bonds, that's on them. If there's consequences...well, that's what the game is about, right?<br /> <br /> Besides, there's all those Devotions that require multiple clan-specific Disciplines. That's a pretty clear mechanical indication that it's expected at least <i>some</i> players (or storyteller characters) would be in a position to learn multiple Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T13:44:23-08:00","id":1166796,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd be more concerned about Blood Adiction than Vindiculim, with a first stage Vindiculim the other kindred who I'm assuming is an ally gains +1 die on some rolls against you, a better impression for Social Manovers and harming them is akin to the death of a mortal family member or two weeks without human contact and only lasts a year. Vitae Adiction can lead you to a third stage Vindiculim if anyone found out and the Deprived Condition isn't a lot of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T15:18:18-08:00","id":1166838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1166796#post1166796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae Adiction can lead you to a third stage Vindiculim if anyone found out and the Deprived Condition isn't a lot of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This too. Fake-Love would be an interesting feeling to grapple irl; like a crush dailed all the way up? But addiction. I could do without anymore addiction. \u00ac_\u00ac<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/932461-is-my-clan-discipline-for-yours-as-common-as-pcs-seem-to-expect?p=1166791#post1166791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sure. I never meant to imply I thought it would be <i>common</i>. I was just spitballing simple reasons that could overcome any societal &quot;shunning&quot; or taboo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my mistake. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So we agree then? Society doesn't think much of it, which is often good enough reason for some to do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T17:28:04-08:00","id":1170321,"title":"","content":"So I haven't read the entire thread. I just wanna give my two cents on the original question, even if maybe someone has hit the same points.<br /> <br /> So look at the question from the perspective of a vampire. Vampires are creatures that can, potentially, live forever. There are, essentially, two ways a vampire dies.<br /> <br /> One is they get careless and fall to one of their weaknesses, mainly sunlight. Blood is, all things considered, easy enough for a vampire to get, so dying of, for lack of a better term, starvation, is not, really, a concern. Sunlight is their main natural concern, and even that isn't *that* hard to deal with.<br /> <br /> Most vampires who die their final death do so due to their second problem: unnatural final death. As in something kills them.<br /> <br /> Hunters are a problem, of course. But vampires who manage to survive their first few years are likely clever enough to not fall prey to such a trap. And remember that for most vampires, years are nothing.<br /> <br /> Another potential problem for vamps are other supernaturals. The amount of interaction between supernaturals, admittedly, is gonna depend on how your game is run, but I've usually read the books with an understanding that the different supernatural groups having any interaction between them is rare. So yeah, a vamp may die if some werewolf decides he needs to go. But I don't see that as being a common thing.<br /> <br /> As far as I have ever read the books, it seems to me that the biggest threat to a vampire's continued existence is other vampires. They are naturally selfish, manipulative, and dangerous creatures. A vampire who doesn't immediately interpret other vamps as potential enemies, if not enemies outright, is one who's not gonna survive many nights.<br /> <br /> So consider all of this information. No discipline is necessary, really, for any vamp to survive. They can all hide from the sun and get blood easily enough with their natural abilities, without even tapping into their own disciplines, let alone other clans. And their whole existence, really, is survival. That's the gamble of being a vamp. I can live forever, if only I can avoid my weaknesses and avoid being killed.<br /> <br /> So with all that being considered, consider the risk and reward of trading disciplines. If there's a discipline I, specifically, need to possess for my agenda, then maybe, MAYBE, it is worth it. But that's a big if. What's stopping me from trading a favor for a favor with a vamp who has that discipline? Just because I don't have dominate doesn't mean there isn't a ventrue who needs someone to do his dirty work. And that ventrue would probably be more than willing to dominate this or that person, mortal or vamp, in exchange for me using, say, my auspex to find some information out for him.<br /> <br /> But as far as trading disciplines, remember the number one cause, as far as my interpretation, of vampire death is other vampires. Maybe not by fist to fist violence. But manipulation and deceit and all that good vampire stuff. And vampire alliances are fragile things. So just because this vamp is my ally at this exact moment doesn't mean he will be in 100, 50, or even 10 years. And giving him access to my clan discipline right now is giving him a tool that might be potentially turned against me later.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying vamps trading disciplines doesn't happen or make no sense. I could especially see it being common between younger vampires who still think in human terms and don't have this kind of &quot;everyone is either a tool or a potential enemy&quot; mentality. But older vamps are likely to be more cautious and more likely to deal in temporary alliances than to give potential rivals tools that can be used against them a long ways down the line. The longer a vamp lives, the less likely he or she is to think in terms of wanting to acquire power. That's a human concern. Vampires are concerned with survival. It's why the beast is so scary. Because it is what all vampires tend towards: pure survival instinct. Power, really is only a means to that end. A vampire straight out of character creation is powerful to a degree that we really can't conceive of as humans. Hell, a ventrue who puts all his starting dots into dominate can literally end the world by dominating his way into the white house and having the president launch all the nukes. Power is something tempting to us humans, but vamps are parasites. They don't need power. And the longer they exist, the more they realize that. They just need to survive. Everything they do is geared towards that one hope of immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}